# Build output
/target
# The measurement probes under scripts/ are their own cargo workspaces, so they
# build into their own target dirs that the root-anchored rule above misses.
# Committed here on the release branch rather than on one feature branch: three
# separate commits swept ~500 build artifacts each before this existed.
# The code-size probe is its own workspace (see scripts/codesize/Cargo.toml),
# so it builds into its own target dir that the root-anchored rule above misses.
/scripts/codesize/target
/scripts/cycles/target
# The cycle probe's Cargo.lock IS committed (unlike this comment's earlier
# advice). The counts it produces are documented reference evidence measured
# in a pinned environment, the reference image preloads dependencies from the
# lockfile at build time, and the release checklist stages it -- an unpinned
# probe dependency was the one hole left in the environment.
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, IDE, and AI/agent tooling state.
#
# These are per-developer settings, not project configuration. They were
# previously covered only by individual developers' global git config, which
# left a fresh clone free to commit them.
#
# Shared project config lives at the repo root and is tracked deliberately:
# AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .cargo/config.toml, deny.toml, rust-toolchain.toml.
# To share something from an ignored directory, add a negation below rather
# than relying on `git add -f`, so the decision is visible in the diff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# AI / agent tooling
.claude/
.cursor/
.cursorignore
.cursorrules
.windsurf/
.aider*
.continue/
.codeium/
.github/copilot-instructions.local.md

# IDEs and editors
.idea/
.vscode/
.zed/
.fleet/
.helix/
*.iml
*.code-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.sublime-project
.sublime-workspace

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
